  "text": "Baдe 18/1 1292k 80:55 50 0050 009 ear Creek\nBMP: PAVING\n1. METHODS: Paving is required on private roads, driveways and parking\nareas when they are accessed by a paved road. Parking areas and drives must\nbe paved with a minimum of 6 inches of road base compacted to 95% modified\nProctor and 3 inches of asphalt, see figure. Paved parking areas for all other\ndevelopment shall be designed in accordance with Section 2.43. C, with TI\nequaling 6.0, as per Clear Creek County's Roadway Design and Construction\nManual.\nThe County may also require pavement that drinks, or porous pavement. This\nrequirement will be contingent upon any land use case stipulation/condition and will be\ndesigned by a Colorado licensed engineer.\n2.\nMATERIALS:\n3\" asphalt, 3\"base course, 3\" subbase, as per figure 6, Clear Creek County's\nRoadway Design and Construction Manual.\n3.\nMAINTENANCE TIPS:\nReplace/repair as required.\n4.\nTEMPORARY OR PERMANENT USE: Paving is a temporary and\nPermanent BMP.\nSHOUL DER\nGRAVEL\nSHOUL DER\nGRAVEL\nDRIVING\nLANE\n- 10'\n2%\nDRIVING\nLANE\n— 10'\n2%\n3:1\n4:1\n3\" ASPHALT\n8 3\" BASE COURSE\n% 3\" SUBBASE T\nTypical Cross Section for a Primitive Status Road\n118",
